I don't know, I'd have to agree that being addressed by my last name
only is quite rude- unless I know the person doing the addressing well
(and even in that case, it might be rude). If a complete stranger (or
even someone I didn't know particularly well, but had met before)
addressed me by last name only, it would rub me the wrong way-
partially because I think that that sort of thing implies a certain
amount of familiarity. On the other hand, I'm from the Midwest, which
has strong Scandinavian and German heritage, so that may be part of
the reason why. While I am addressed occasionally as "Mr." even by
people I know well, the use of the last name just seems odd and rude
to me in general; if I don't know someone at all, they ought to use
"Mr." plus last name, and chances are that I'll say "Just call me
Jeff".

